@startuml Camera Frame Processing
title Camera Frame Processing - ESP32 to Mobile App

note over Camera, App
  **Technologies Used:**
  • OV2640 - 2MP camera module with JPEG encoder
  • PSRAM - External RAM for buffering large images
  • MQTT - Publish/Subscribe messaging protocol
  • JPEG - Image format with 0xFFD8 header
  • Base64 - Binary-to-text encoding for WebSocket
  • WebSocket - Real-time bidirectional communication
end note

participant "ESP32 Camera\n(OV2640)" as Camera
participant "ESP32\n(PSRAM)" as ESP
participant "MQTT Broker" as MQTT
participant "Backend\nCamera Handler" as Backend
participant "Backend\nBuffer" as Buffer
participant "WebSocket" as WS
participant "Mobile App" as App

== Frame Capture on ESP32 ==
Camera -> ESP: Capture photo
ESP -> ESP: Get JPEG buffer from camera
ESP -> ESP: Store frame in PSRAM
ESP -> ESP: Check frame size

alt Large frame (needs splitting)
    ESP -> ESP: Split into ~4KB parts
    ESP -> ESP: Generate frame_id
    
    loop For each part
        ESP -> MQTT: Publish to {mac}/device/camera/frame/{frame_id}/part/{n}
        MQTT -> Backend: Forward part {n}
        Backend -> Buffer: Store part {n} in memory
        
        alt Part fails to send
            ESP -> ESP: Keep in cache
            note right: Will retry on next flush
        end
    end
    
    ESP -> MQTT: Publish to {mac}/device/camera/frame/{frame_id}/end
    MQTT -> Backend: Forward /end marker
    
else Small frame (single message)
    ESP -> MQTT: Publish entire frame to {mac}/device/camera/frame/{frame_id}
    MQTT -> Backend: Forward complete frame
end

== Frame Assembly on Backend ==
Backend -> Backend: Receive /end marker
Backend -> Buffer: Retrieve all parts for frame_id
Backend -> Backend: Sort parts by part number
Backend -> Backend: Concatenate parts into single buffer
Backend -> Backend: Validate JPEG format\n(check 0xFFD8 header)

alt Valid JPEG
    Backend -> Backend: Optionally save to disk\n(frame_{index}_{timestamp}.jpg)
    Backend -> Backend: Convert to Base64
    Backend -> WS: Send camera_frame event\n{timestamp, image_base64, format: "jpg"}
    WS -> App: Forward camera frame
    App -> App: Decode Base64
    App -> App: Display frame
    
    Backend -> Buffer: Clear frame_id buffer
    
else Invalid JPEG or incomplete
    Backend -> Backend: Log error
    Backend -> Buffer: Ignore and discard
end

alt Buffer overflow (too many fragments)
    Backend -> Buffer: Check buffer size
    Backend -> Buffer: Clear old/incomplete frames
    note right: Prevent memory issues
end

@enduml